            <!-- ================= SUMMARY ================= -->
            <div class="alert alert-primary mb-4">

                <h2 class="h5 fw-bold">
                    Summary
                </h2>

                <p>
                    Polymorphism means
                    <strong>one thing having many forms</strong>.
                    It allows the same method or reference to behave differently
                    depending on the situation.
                </p>

                <p>
                    C# supports compile-time polymorphism through method
                    overloading and run-time polymorphism through method overriding.
                </p>

                <p class="mb-0">
                    Understanding polymorphism is essential for developing
                    flexible, reusable, and maintainable object-oriented applications.
                </p>

            </div>


